think The genuinely new crux none of the agree-on-order/supply/quorum/rotation arcs touched is PLACEMENT — which host runs which world. The hard-but-tractable decisive move: a placement that is a pure function of the fleet, invariant under arrival order, so no central scheduler is trusted (the leaderless answer the season already keeps, applied one layer down). Method: highest weave-score (rendezvous/HRW), SHA-256(domain · world-id · host-pk), chosen over hash-mod-count for minimal disruption (which becomes r2's convergence).
think Self-approved the design read (active-designing/20260813-114651_…), then wrote mycelium/puddle.rye following the warrant.rye idiom exactly — opening triad, named errors, ≥2 asserts per fn with // invariant, bounded Fleet (max_hosts 16 · max_worlds 64 · world_id_len 24), copy_disjoint not @memcpy, no compound asserts, u32 widths, pure fixed buffers (main() !void, no arena).
think The berth is derived never written (no set_berth); worlds processed in canonical id order (bounded selection sort); each takes the highest-weave-score host with remaining capacity; ties (never seen with SHA-256) break on the greater public key, never on insertion index — so arrival-order independence holds even in the impossible case.
